  "body": "Porting from https://www.w3.org/Bugs/Public/show_bug.cgi?id=28921. There @birtles notes that\r\n\r\n> In summary, some sites are calling load() on preload=\"none\" resources and expecting to get a \"loadedmetadata\" event even though the spec doesn't require this.\r\n\r\nIt appears at least some browsers have implemented something contrary to the current spec, that is more compatible with web site expectations. The linked bug contains some ideas of how this might work. We need tests.",
